  onboarding:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: User Onboarding
    triggers:
    - onboard
    - onboarding
    - setup profile
    - first time
    - new user
    - onboard application --app-name
    response_type: interactive
    expected_orchestrator: OnboardingOrchestrator
    operation_name: Onboarding
    understanding_content: "You're starting the onboarding process to personalize CORTEX for your experience level, interaction preferences, and tech stack."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - This quick 3-question setup helps CORTEX adapt to your needs."
    response_content: |
      Welcome! Let's personalize CORTEX in ~30 seconds.
      
      **Required Parameter:** `--app-name <name>`  
      Example: `onboard application --app-name MyProject`
      
      **What we'll capture:**
      1. Your application name (required for context and personalization)
      2. Your experience level (affects explanation depth)
      3. Your interaction preference (autonomous/guided/educational/pair)
      4. Your tech stack context (optional - for deployment recommendations)
      
      **Important:** Tech stack is context for deployment, NOT a constraint.  
      CORTEX will always recommend the best solution first.
      
      **Note:** First-time setup may take 10-15 minutes if shared environment needs to be created.
      You'll see step-by-step progress (Step 1/7, 2/7, etc.) during setup.
      
      {onboarding_question}
    request_echo_content: "Set up CORTEX profile with application name"
    next_steps_content: |
      Provide --app-name parameter: onboard application --app-name <YourProjectName>
      Answer the current question to proceed.
      You can update your profile anytime with `update profile`.
  
  regenerate_diagrams:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Diagram Regeneration
    triggers:
    - regenerate diagram
    - refresh diagram
    - update diagram
    - diagram sync
    - rebuild diagram
    - diagram regeneration
    response_type: detailed
    expected_orchestrator: DiagramRegenerationOrchestrator
    operation_name: Diagram Regeneration
    understanding_content: "You want to regenerate architecture diagrams from source code to reflect the current system structure."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - Diagram regeneration automatically analyzes code structure and relationships to produce up-to-date visual documentation."
    response_content: |
      **Diagram Regeneration Process:**
      
      1. **Code Analysis** - Scan source files to extract components, relationships, dependencies
      2. **Structure Detection** - Identify orchestrators, agents, modules, workflows
      3. **Relationship Mapping** - Trace calls, imports, and data flows
      4. **Diagram Generation** - Produce Mermaid diagrams (flowcharts, class diagrams, sequence diagrams)
      5. **File Updates** - Save diagrams to documentation directory
      
      **Generated Diagrams:**
      • System architecture overview
      • Component relationships
      • Data flow diagrams
      • Module dependencies
    request_echo_content: "Regenerate architecture diagrams from current source code"
    next_steps_content: |
      Say "regenerate diagram" to start the automated diagram generation process.
      
      Diagrams will be saved to `docs/architecture/` directory.
  
  resume_conversation:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Resume Conversation
    triggers:
    - resume
    - continue
    - restore
    - resume conversation
    - continue conversation
    response_type: interactive
    operation_name: Resume Conversation
    understanding_content: "You want to resume a previous conversation with full context restoration."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - CORTEX restores conversation history, entity extraction, and working context from Tier 1 memory."
    response_content: |
      **Context Restoration Process:**
      
      1. **Conversation Retrieval** - Load conversation from Tier 1 working memory
      2. **Entity Extraction** - Restore extracted entities (files, functions, concepts)
      3. **Context Injection** - Rebuild working context with relevant code/docs
      4. **Continuation** - Resume exactly where you left off
      
      **What's Restored:**
      • Full conversation history
      • Extracted entities and relationships
      • Active tasks and progress
      • File references and code context
    request_echo_content: "Resume previous conversation with context"
    next_steps_content: |
      Provide conversation ID: `resume {conversation_id}`
      Or describe the topic: `resume the authentication work`
  
  admin_feedback_review:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Admin Feedback Review
    triggers:
    - admin feedback
    - review feedback
    - admin feedback review
    response_type: detailed
    operation_name: Admin Feedback Review
    understanding_content: "You want to review collected user feedback for CORTEX improvements."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - Admin operation for reviewing and analyzing user feedback submissions."
    response_content: |
      **Feedback Review Dashboard:**
      
      1. **Recent Feedback** - Display latest user submissions
      2. **Category Breakdown** - Group by bug/feature/improvement
      3. **Priority Analysis** - Identify high-impact items
      4. **Action Items** - Generate improvement tasks
      
      **Review Capabilities:**
      • Filter by severity, category, date
      • View user context and screenshots
      • Track resolution status
      • Export for planning
    request_echo_content: "Review user feedback submissions"
    next_steps_content: |
      Say "admin feedback review" to access the feedback dashboard.
      Admin-only operation (requires CORTEX development context).
  
  feedback_report:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Feedback Report
    triggers:
    - feedback
    - report
    - report issue
    - bug report
    - feedback report
    response_type: interactive
    operation_name: Feedback Report
    understanding_content: "You want to submit feedback about CORTEX (bug, feature request, or improvement)."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - Your feedback helps improve CORTEX for everyone."
    response_content: |
      **Feedback Submission Process:**
      
      1. **Category Selection** - Bug / Feature Request / Improvement
      2. **Context Collection** - Auto-capture system state, conversation ID
      3. **Privacy Protection** - Auto-redact sensitive data
      4. **GitHub Gist Upload** - Share with CORTEX team
      
      **What We Capture:**
      • Feedback description (your input)
      • System context (CORTEX version, environment)
      • Conversation ID (if relevant)
      • Redacted examples (no sensitive data)
    request_echo_content: "Submit feedback to improve CORTEX"
    next_steps_content: |
      Say "feedback" to start the guided submission process.
      Your privacy is protected - sensitive data is automatically redacted.
  
  cortex_tutorial:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: CORTEX Tutorial
    triggers:
    - tutorial
    - demo
    - show me
    - cortex tutorial
    - interactive demo
    response_type: interactive
    operation_name: CORTEX Tutorial
    understanding_content: "You want an interactive demonstration of CORTEX capabilities."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - Hands-on tutorial walks through real CORTEX features with live execution."
    response_content: |
      **Interactive Tutorial Program:**
      
      **Duration:** 15-30 minutes (customizable)
      **Format:** Build real feature with tests and production-ready code
      
      **What You'll Learn:**
      1. **Planning System 2.0** - DoR/DoD validation, Vision API
      2. **TDD Mastery** - RED→GREEN→REFACTOR workflow
      3. **Auto-Debug** - Automatic debug session on test failures
      4. **Brain Protection** - SKULL rules and governance
      5. **Git Isolation** - Safe CORTEX/user code separation
      
      **Tutorial Modes:**
      • Quick (15 min) - Core features only
      • Standard (25 min) - Full walkthrough
      • Comprehensive (30 min) - Deep dive with best practices
    request_echo_content: "Start interactive CORTEX tutorial"
    next_steps_content: |
      Say "tutorial" to start the guided walkthrough.
      Choose your mode: "tutorial quick", "tutorial standard", or "tutorial comprehensive".
  
  environment_setup:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Environment Setup
    triggers:
    - setup
    - environment
    - configure
    - environment setup
    - setup environment
    response_type: detailed
    operation_name: Environment Setup
    understanding_content: "You want to configure CORTEX development environment on your machine."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - Automated setup for Mac/Windows/Linux with dependency management."
    response_content: |
      **Environment Setup Process:**
      
      1. **Platform Detection** - Auto-detect Mac/Windows/Linux
      2. **Dependency Check** - Verify Python 3.8+, Git, required packages
      3. **Brain Initialization** - Create Tier 1/2/3 databases
      4. **Git Configuration** - Setup .gitignore, hooks
      5. **Validation** - Test all components
      
      **What Gets Configured:**
      • Python environment (venv or system)
      • CORTEX brain databases (SQLite)
      • Git isolation rules
