  optimize_system:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Optimize System
    triggers:
    - optimize
    - optimize cortex
    - optimize system
    - clean and optimize
    response_type: detailed
    understanding_content: "You want to optimize CORTEX system performance by cleaning brain databases, removing outdated cache entries, and compacting SQLite files."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - Optimization is a safe, non-destructive operation with automatic backups."
    response_content: "**Optimization Process:**\n   \n   1. **Brain Database Cleaning** - Removes outdated conversation entries (70-conversation FIFO)\n   2. **Cache Cleanup** - Clears expired cache entries and orphaned data\n   3. **SQLite Vacuuming** - Compacts Tier 1, Tier 2, and Tier 3 databases\n   4. **Performance Validation** - Verifies query performance (<100ms requirement)\n   \n   **Expected Results:**\n   • Space savings: 50-200 MB typical\n   • Query performance: <100ms (Tier 1), <500ms (Tier 2/3)\n   • Database integrity: Validated after optimization\n   • Cache effectiveness: 6.4x speedup maintained\n   \n   **Safety Features:**\n   • Automatic backup before optimization\n   • Read-only operations during validation\n   • Rollback capability if issues detected"
    request_echo_content: "Optimize CORTEX system (clean databases, vacuum SQLite, improve performance)"
    next_steps_content: "**Optimization Complete:**\n   \n   1. ✅ Check space savings reported above\n   2. ✅ Verify query performance metrics\n   3. ✅ Run `healthcheck` to validate system integrity\n   4. ✅ Continue normal CORTEX operations\n   \n   **Performance Monitoring:**\n   Use `cache status` to check effectiveness metrics after optimization."

  workflow_execution:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Workflow Execution
    triggers:
    - workflow
    - execute workflow
    - run workflow
    - start workflow
    response_type: detailed

  git_checkpoint:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Git Checkpoint
    triggers:
    - git checkpoint
    - create checkpoint
    - save checkpoint
    response_type: detailed
    handler: src.orchestrators.git_checkpoint_orchestrator.GitCheckpointOrchestrator

  commit_operation:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Commit and Sync
    triggers:
    - commit
    - commit and push
    - sync with origin
    - commit sync
    - push changes
    - sync repository
    - commit and sync
    - git sync
    - push to origin
    - push to remote
    - pull and push
    - sync repo
    - sync code
    - update remote
    - push code
    - commit changes
    - save and push
    - upload changes
    - sync with remote
    - push commits
    - send changes
    - publish changes
    response_type: detailed
    expected_orchestrator: CommitOrchestrator
    handler: src.orchestrators.commit_orchestrator.CommitOrchestrator
    understanding_content: "You want to synchronize your local repository with origin by pulling, merging, and pushing changes while ensuring no untracked files remain."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - Commit workflow will handle pre-flight validation, untracked files, merge conflicts, and create safety checkpoints automatically."
    response_content: "**Commit Workflow Steps:**\n   \n   1. **Pre-flight Check** - Validate current repository state\n   2. **Handle Untracked Files** - Prompt to add or ignore untracked files\n   3. **Commit Local Changes** - Create commit with auto-generated or custom message\n   4. **Create Checkpoint** - Safety checkpoint for rollback capability\n   5. **Pull from Origin** - Fetch and merge/rebase with remote changes\n   6. **Push to Origin** - Upload merged changes to remote repository\n   \n   **Safety Features:**\n   • Git checkpoint before pull (rollback if needed)\n   • Merge conflict detection with clear guidance\n   • Untracked file validation (zero untracked files guarantee)\n   • Progress reporting for each step"
    request_echo_content: "Sync repository with origin (pull, merge, push)"
    next_steps_content: "**Execution Options:**\n   \n   1. **Standard Sync** - Say \"commit\" to start with interactive prompts\n   2. **Auto-add Untracked** - Say \"commit --auto-add\" to automatically stage untracked files\n   3. **Rebase Strategy** - Say \"commit --rebase\" to use rebase instead of merge\n   4. **Custom Message** - Say \"commit --message 'your message'\" for custom commit message\n   \n   **Rollback Safety:**\n   If issues occur, say \"rollback to checkpoint\" to restore pre-sync state.\n   \n   Ready to sync? Say \"commit\" to begin."

  rollback_operation:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: Rollback to Checkpoint
    triggers:
    - rollback
    - rollback to
    - restore to checkpoint
    - undo to checkpoint
    - revert to checkpoint
    response_type: detailed
    expected_orchestrator: RollbackOrchestrator
    handler: src.orchestrators.rollback_orchestrator.RollbackOrchestrator
    understanding_content: "You want to rollback your repository to a previous checkpoint created during TDD workflow (pre-work, tdd-red, tdd-green, refactoring, post-work)."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - Rollback will validate checkpoint exists, check for uncommitted changes, show diff preview, and require confirmation before executing."
    response_content: "**Rollback Workflow Steps:**\n   \n   1. **Checkpoint Validation** - Verify checkpoint exists in PhaseCheckpointManager\n   2. **Safety Checks** - Detect uncommitted changes and merge conflicts\n   3. **Preview Changes** - Show git diff of changes to be discarded\n   4. **User Confirmation** - Require explicit 'yes' confirmation\n   5. **Execute Rollback** - Run git reset --hard to checkpoint\n   \n   **Safety Features:**\n   • Blocks rollback if uncommitted changes exist\n   • Blocks rollback if merge in progress\n   • Shows diff preview before confirmation\n   • Dry-run mode (--dry-run) for preview without execution\n   • Force mode (--force) to bypass safety checks (DANGER: loses changes)\n   \n   **Checkpoint Types:**\n   • pre-work - Before starting feature work\n   • tdd-red - After writing failing test\n   • tdd-green - After making test pass\n   • refactoring - After code cleanup\n   • post-work - After completing feature"
    request_echo_content: "Rollback to previous checkpoint"
    next_steps_content: "**Execution Options:**\n   \n   1. **Safe Rollback** - Say \"rollback to <checkpoint-id>\" for full safety workflow\n   2. **Preview Only** - Say \"rollback to <checkpoint-id> --dry-run\" to see diff without executing\n   3. **Force Rollback** - Say \"rollback to <checkpoint-id> --force\" to bypass safety (⚠️ loses uncommitted changes)\n   \n   **Finding Checkpoints:**\n   • Say \"list checkpoints\" to see available checkpoint IDs\n   • Checkpoint IDs follow format: phase-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS (e.g., tdd-green-20251129-140000)\n   \n   **Resolution Tips:**\n   • If uncommitted changes block rollback: commit or stash first\n   • If merge in progress: complete merge or abort with \"git merge --abort\"\n   \n   Ready to rollback? Provide checkpoint ID or say \"list checkpoints\" to see options."

  ado_planning:
    <<: *standard_5_part_base
    name: ADO Work Item Planning
    triggers:
    - plan ado
    - ado story
    - ado feature
    - create ado work item
    - estimate work item
    response_type: detailed
    expected_orchestrator: SWAGGEREntryPointOrchestrator
    handler: src.orchestrators.swagger_entry_point_orchestrator.SWAGGEREntryPointOrchestrator
    understanding_content: "You want to create Azure DevOps work items (stories, features, tasks) with Definition of Ready validation and story point estimation."
    challenge_content: "No Challenge - ADO planning enforces DoR (Definition of Ready) validation before providing estimates to ensure requirements are complete."
    response_content: "**ADO Planning Workflow:**\n   \n   1. **DoR Validation** - Interactive questioning across 5 categories (requirements, dependencies, technical, security, testing)\n   2. **Work Item Decomposition** - Break down Epics → Features → Stories → Tasks\n   3. **Story Point Estimation** - Modified Fibonacci scale (1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13)\n   4. **Timeframe Analysis** - Parallel track identification, team size scenarios, critical path\n   5. **ADO Output** - Copy-paste ready markdown with acceptance criteria"
    request_echo_content: "Create ADO work items with DoR validation"
    next_steps_content: "Ready to start? Provide feature name or say \"plan ado [feature name]\" to begin."

